# enscribe

enscribe is an academic publishing system built on HTML, CSS, and
JavaScript, with a compact shorthand for authoring. You write in a terse,
uniform tag syntax; enscribe compiles it to clean, semantic Layer 1 HTML
that a stylesheet themes into a finished document.

This documentation site is itself authored in enscribe and rendered by the
toolchain — the site you are reading is dogfooding the system.

## Explore

- [Quickstart](quickstart.html) — try enscribe live in your browser: edit
  source on the left, watch the rendered output on the right.
- [Example article](example-article.html) — a rendered, read-only page, with
  a link to its enscribe source on GitHub.

## Status

This is **placeholder** content for the Phase 14 Slice 3a framework, which
builds the static-site machinery. The real homepage, a Quickstart guide, and
articles translating the project's README and DESIGN land in later slices.
